1. e4 e5 2. Qh5 {This move violates the golden opening rules: it neither occupies the centre nor develops a piece meaningfully.} Nc6 (2...
Nf6 {Although this gives up a pawn and is of course not the best move, Black is not even worse here!} 3. Qxe5+ Be7 $44 {Black gets a great deal of time for the pawn.} 4. d3 d5 $1 5. exd5 O-O $15 {And suddenly Black is even better.}) 3. Bc4 {White has only one threat, nothing more.} g6 (3... Nf6 $4 {Check active moves.} 4. Qxf7#) 4. Qf3 Nf6
5. Qb3 $2 {White commits everything to the attack, but has not developed a single piece and has moved only the queen several times.} (5. Ne2 Bg7 {[%cal Ge8g8,Yf7f5,Yg8h8] Bg7 is not ideally placed, but overall Black is better. Simply castle and switch to a kingside setup.}) 5... Nd4 {An active move that wins the game immediately.} 6. Bxf7+ (6. Qd3 d5 $1 {The centre is decisive.} 7. exd5 Bf5 {An active move, stronger than Nxd5.} 8. Qc3 Nxc2+ $19) (6. Qc3 Nxe4) (6. Qe3 Nxc2+) 6... Ke7
7. Qc4 b5 $19 {White cannot keep Bf7 defended.} *

